    "question": {
      ":question/id": "04c1f322-52de-542b-bd7d-195605a76096",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -5 & -9 \\\\ 10 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}39 & 0 & -29 \\\\ -42 & 0 & 36 \\\\ 10 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{32}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -5 & -9 \\\\ 10 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}+4R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}39 & 0 & -29 \\\\ 8 & -5 & -9 \\\\ 10 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}-5R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}39 & 0 & -29 \\\\ -42 & 0 & 36 \\\\ 10 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}+4R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}-5R_{3}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
